  "question": {
    "text": "A <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> amplifier, has a power gain of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>dB</mi></math> . The input resistance and output load resistance are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>k</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> respectively. Find the value of common-emitter current gain.<br />\r[Take gain in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>dB</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>log</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math>]"
  },
